---
import "@skryensya/core/components/tile.css";
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import ComponentPreview from "../../../components/ComponentPreview.astro";
import { switchTree, tileSwitchTree } from "../../../demos/switch";
import { getLocale, useTranslations } from "../../../i18n";
import StylingHooks from "../../../components/StylingHooks.astro";

const t = useTranslations(getLocale(Astro.url));


const tileSwitchVanilla = `import { initComponents } from "@skryensya/vanilla/auto";

// Each label is authored with data-sk-tile-switch (data-name, data-value,
// data-default-checked) plus its role="switch" input and its indicator.
// initComponents hydrates them with the @zag-js/checkbox machine.
await initComponents();

for (const root of document.querySelectorAll(
  "[data-sk-tile-switch]",
)) {
  root.addEventListener("sk:checkedchange", (event) => {
    console.log(root.dataset.value, event.detail.checked);
  });
}`;

---

<Base title="Switch" description="Switch: A persistent binary preference over native checkbox.">
  <h1>Switch</h1>
  <p class="lede">A binary state that takes effect immediately: on or off. For a selection that requires saving, use Checkbox.</p>

  <ComponentPreview tree={switchTree(t)} label="Switch" />
  <p>Does not require vanilla initialization: the native checkbox preserves keyboard, reset and form submit. React only encapsulates that same control.</p>

  <h2>Surface switch: TileSwitch</h2>
  <p>
    When the preference needs a title, a description, and the whole surface as target, use
    <code>TileSwitch</code>. It's the same control (<code>sk-switch__control</code> + thumb); only
    the container changes, the same relationship <code>TileCheckbox</code> has to Checkbox.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview tree={tileSwitchTree(t)} label="TileSwitch" />
  <p>The <code>tile-switch</code> enhancer (Svelte + <code>@zag-js/checkbox</code>, the same machine as TileCheckbox and React) hydrates each <code>data-sk-tile-switch</code> label with <code>initComponents()</code>: it controls its (hidden, <code>role="switch"</code>) <code>input[data-part="input"]</code> and syncs <code>data-state</code>; the <code>[data-part="indicator"]</code> is the visual control.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={tileSwitchVanilla} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of the preview.</p>

  <h2>Contract</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The input is still <code>checkbox</code>; <code>role="switch"</code> communicates the correct semantics.</li>
    <li><code>defaultChecked</code> leaves the value to the browser; <code>checked</code> controls it.</li>
    <li><code>onCheckedChange</code> (<code>onCheck</code> on TileSwitch) reports the intent; it does not infer persistence or make requests.</li>
    <li>Use only if the change takes effect immediately and there are exactly two states: no indeterminate, unlike Checkbox.</li>
    <li>TileSwitch reuses <code>sk-switch__control</code> and the same thumb; it does not invent another control.</li>
  </ul>
  <StylingHooks groups={[{ file: "components/switch.css", probe: "sk-switch" }]} />
</Base>
